@startuml
title An accepted proposal is saved now and applied at period close
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam maxMessageSize 170
participant "Budget graph" as Graph
database "App DB" as DB
database "Budget checkpoint DB" as CP
actor User
participant "Decision service + API\nfrontend in progress" as Decisions
participant "PLANNED\nPeriod-close service" as Close
Graph -> DB : Store pending_user alert\n+ linked advice + proposed cents
Graph -> CP : interrupt(waiting_for alert IDs)
Graph -> DB : Run status = awaiting_user
User -> Decisions : Accept or dismiss alert
Decisions -> DB : Check ownership + pending status
Decisions -> DB : Commit alert.status\n+ advice_log.outcome
note over DB, CP
Decision and checkpoint are separate writes.
The saved decision must survive a failed resume.
end note
Decisions -> CP : Read waiting IDs
Decisions -> Graph : resume_budget_run(alert_id, decision)
alt Other proposals remain
  Graph -> CP : interrupt again
else All proposals decided
  Graph -> DB : persist_state -> ok\nrecord decisions
end
note over Graph, Decisions
Acceptance does not change today's limit.
Graph resume records completion;
the decision service saves alert status.
end note
== At period end: planned orchestration ==
Close -> DB : Load final actuals + accepted proposals
Close -> Close : Existing pure close_period function:\naccepted number wins; otherwise fixed actual\nor 70% old + 30% actual, clamped +/-15%
Close -> DB : PLANNED atomic close old period\n+ create next period and lines
note over Decisions, Close
Still specify recovery after failed resume,
late decisions, and conflicting proposals.
end note
@enduml
